    "answer": {
      "short": "$28\\text{ m}$",
      "worked": "Base side length:\n$$\\begin{align*}s&=\\sqrt{1764}\\\\s&=42\\text{ m}\\end{align*}$$\nArea of each triangular face:\n$$\\begin{align*}A&=\\frac{4704-1764}{4}\\\\A&=735\\text{ m}^2\\end{align*}$$\nSlant height:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac12\\times42\\times l&=735\\\\l&=35\\text{ m}\\end{align*}$$\nThe distance from the centre of the base to the midpoint of a base edge is $42\\div2=21\\text{ m}$. By Pythagoras:\n$$\\begin{align*}h^2&=35^2-21^2\\\\h^2&=784\\\\h&=28\\text{ m}\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
